explanation  : The capture shows broadcast 802.11 management frames with Frame Control 0xc0 (type=0 mgmt, subtype=12 deauthentication) and 0xa0 (subtype=10 disassociation), sent to ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff with a spoofed AP address in a 1s window — a classic deauth/disassoc flood that forcibly drops OT/ICS stations off the WLAN. The filter parses only the Frame Control field, extracting type bits [3:2] and subtype bits [7:4], and drops any management frame whose subtype is 12 (deauth) or 10 (disassoc), so it matches on frame structure rather than exact bytes. Beacons (subtype 8) and data frames pass unchanged; harness result: TPR=1.000 FPR=0.000 with gcc -Wall -std=c11 clean.
